>2006</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>2594</fpage><lpage>2601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16427163</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.vaccine.2005.12.015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christenson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bottiger</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measles antibody: comparison of long-term vaccination titres, early vaccination titres and naturally acquired immunity to and booster effects on the measles virus</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><year>1994</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>133</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8147093</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0264-410X(94)90049-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davidkin</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Valle</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Vaccine-induced measles virus antibodies after two doses of combined measles, mumps and rubella vaccine: a 12-year follow-up in two cohorts</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><year>1998</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>2052</fpage><lpage>2057</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9796064</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0264-410X(98)00081-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pebody</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gay</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hesketh</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vyse</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan-Capner</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Litton</surname>